\begin{tabular}{llc}
\toprule
Sparsity & Method & C4 PPL$\downarrow$ \\
\midrule
0\% & Dense & 9.21 \\
\midrule
30\% & KL predictor (Ours) & \textbf{16.03$\pm$0.01} \\ % exp_id: c4_ood_kl30_s42, c4_ood_kl30_s123
\midrule
\multirow{2}{*}{50\%} & KL predictor (Ours) & \textbf{18.40} \\ % exp_id: eval_c4_ood_kl50
& TEAL vanilla & 38.75 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

At the 30\% sparsity level, the KL predictor achieves C4 PPL 16.03$\pm$0.01 (2-seed, $1.74\times$ dense), confirming OOD generalization.
At 50\%, the KL predictor achieves 52.5\% relative advantage over TEAL (18.40 vs.\ 38.75), comparable to the 51\% advantage on WikiText-2 (11.79 vs.\ 23.90), confirming that KL-trained predictions generalize across distributions.


